 "honesty": [
  "the nesting rule's first run rejected 24/24 valid FVs: the FS-GUID registry lookup was case-sensitive while spi_map._guid returns uppercase \u2014 the rule worked, the registry had the bug; both the bug and the catch are registered",
  "the FTYPE table was written from memory first and was wrong from 0x0A on; corrected by copying ovmf_census.py's proven table verbatim \u2014 the discipline caught it before the numbers were read",
  "$BSP (AMD BIOS directory) has zero hits on both specimens; $PSP hits exist (26 MSI / 13 GB) but were not parsed this ring \u2014 the PSP lens stays an open front",
  "GB's NVRAM region (0xe40000, 6 freeform files) is walked at file level only; the EVSA store walk is day-0 inventory work",
  "named-share is UI-section coverage, not semantic coverage: 77.5 % MSI / 84.7 % GB \u2014 the unnamed tail is mostly AMI internal freeform blobs"
 ],
 "consequences_day0": [
  "the vendor dump arrives to an instrument with two vendor precedents: flash map by validated nesting, pierce by the LZMA pattern, census by phase, dispatch by postfix grammar",
  "the empty-string dbx tripwire and the trust-store lens are the first checks on the dump's NVRAM region",
  "the swap comparison is now three-way in principle: OVMF builds vs MSI vs Gigabyte \u2014 the vendor report gains a cross-vendor page"
 ]
